Hairy Dragon wrote:
> Is nethack.org the official site?

Yes. It is, for downloading.
For playing, if you want to play on a public server,
it is nao (nethack.alt.org). If you have a sane terminal
emulator, like putty, you can telnet to that site.

If you don't understand how to do it you could download
a package from nethack.org. And then run it there.

I would recommend reading the Guide Book thoroughly,
before starting. It is essential in the beginning, otherwise
you will not know how to play.

Remember Nethack is a very complex and hard game.
It is not meant to be played for a short while. It is meant
to be played forever. To even begin you need to know
a lot. It may be easier to play the tile ports before going
to the terminal one. Although terminal one is easier to
play once you know how to play, the tiled ones are easier
in the beginning as they have menu etc. You can sort
of point and click.

Before entering you should understand whether you
could take a substantial amount of your personal time
and devote to this game. It kind of sucks you inside, and
you tend to stay there. A highly addictive game.

